and scope ledger: 36 physics pairs in `advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry` and 19
purely mathematical support pairs in `quantum-field-theory-mathematics`.
Read `research/plan-advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry-track.md`, the complete
`research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/prose-scaffold.md`, the
exact assigned contracts in `scaffold/proposed-inventory.json`, and all relevant
specialist notes beneath that same dated directory. Its 143 future item
contracts are authoring obligations, not accepted proofs. The three separately
listed unreviewed question candidates are not production items or suppliers.
Only the precisely formulated, source-checked Clay question has an adopted
open-problem classification.

Preserve substantial coverage of Non-Abelian gauge theory, EFT, supersymmetry,
localization, BPS states, generalized symmetries, defects and anomalies through
the source-qualified research frontier. Do not narrow approved claims to avoid
necessary prerequisite work. Build substantial examples on the assigned B
companions; their initial empty canonical item arrays are planning placeholders,
not permission to leave finished pages empty. B-only items cannot supply other
pages. Missing established local proofs are authoring obligations, never newly
invented open problems.

Every technical term needs an explicit mathematical definition with objects,
spaces, maps, regularity, domains, hypotheses and conventions before use. Every
result needs its complete local argument and exact actual supplier uses.
Keep mathematical material purely mathematical; physical deductions use the
physics-theorem or thought-experiment class and explicitly adopted premises.
Preserve the metric, spinor, central-charge, BRST, trace, orientation and
monopole-energy conventions checked in the prose. Continuum path integrals,
localization limits, dualities and physical BPS dictionaries do not follow from
finite models, formal series, ordinary index theory or Hall identities alone.

The external dependency table records current pins and acceptance limits.
Published labels, matching import hashes and judge-only/precheck stamps do not
grant proof acceptance. Resolve each conditional supplier use honestly before
claiming readiness: inspect the actual proof, identify the smallest missing
mathematical result, provide a complete new local mathematical alternative when
appropriate, or escalate to root with precise consumers and the missing
interface. Never edit imported snapshots or original root mathematics. The
existing import receipt identifies the actual original source repository;
source reading is read-only and is not an import or acceptance receipt.

