158-1. **Higher-dimensional categorical anomaly classification.** For a fixed unitary fusion 2-category of codimension-one defects in a 3+1D theory, specify which background/junction data are gaugeable modulo local 4D counterterms and whether the complete obstruction is represented by a 4+1D invertible theory for the fixed tangential structure. The finite \(\mathrm{Vec}_G^\omega\) and \(2\mathrm{Vect}_G^\omega\) algebraic models are examples, not a universal answer.
