## Statement

Assume $\mathrm{AC}_\omega$ as required by the selected trace-class BPS-index data. Use the physical charge datum on a regular pure-SU(2) Seiberg–Witten patch and let $u_-$ and $u_+$ be points in two chambers. Write $\Omega_u(\gamma)$ for its second-helicity supertrace and $\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_{\mathrm{DSZ}}$ for its integral antisymmetric pairing. The finite-field Hall input is a finite acyclic quiver $Q$ over $\mathbb F_q$, $q>1$, with the subobject-first, total-dimension-completed skew Hall generator from the mathematical supplier. Let

$$\chi_Q(\mathbf d,\mathbf e)=\sum_{i\in Q_0}d_i e_i-\sum_{a:i\to j}d_i e_j,\qquad \langle\mathbf d,\mathbf e\rangle_Q=\chi_Q(\mathbf d,\mathbf e)-\chi_Q(\mathbf e,\mathbf d),\qquad t=\sqrt q>0.$$

Suppose an additive map $\rho:\mathbb Z^{Q_0}\to\Gamma_{\mathrm{SW}}$ and a pointed physical charge cone $\Gamma_+$ are supplied such that $\rho(\mathbb N^{Q_0})\subseteq\Gamma_+$, a positive additive degree $\ell$ satisfies $\ell(\rho(\mathbf d))=\sum_i d_i$, and

$$\langle\rho(\mathbf d),\rho(\mathbf e)\rangle_{\mathrm{DSZ}}=\langle\mathbf d,\mathbf e\rangle_Q.$$

For each chamber, suppose a common phase rotation makes the vertex charges $Z_u(\mathbf e_i)=e^{-i\alpha}z_u(\rho(\mathbf e_i))$ lie in the upper half-plane, with the decreasing Hall phase order matching the chosen physical BPS-ray order. Assume the nonzero BPS-index support is locally finite in the $\ell$-completion and $\Omega_u(\gamma)\in\mathbb Z$ on that support.

Let $K_{\mathrm{phys}}$ be a coefficient field containing a fixed $\hbar$ and a field embedding $\sigma:\mathbb Q(t)\to K_{\mathrm{phys}}$ with $\sigma(t)=\hbar$. Define the completed physical charge torus with basis $Y^\gamma$ and multiplication

$$Y^\gamma\star_\hbar Y^\delta=\hbar^{-\langle\delta,\gamma\rangle_{\mathrm{DSZ}}}Y^{\gamma+\delta}.$$

The charge map and coefficient embedding define the degree-continuous torus map $\Phi(x^{\mathbf d})=Y^{\rho(\mathbf d)}$, $\Phi(c x^{\mathbf d})=\sigma(c)Y^{\rho(\mathbf d)}$. On the commutative completed charge series with basis $y^\delta$ for $\delta\in\Gamma_+$, fix a sign refinement $\varepsilon:\Gamma_+\to\{\pm1\}$ satisfying $\varepsilon(\gamma+\delta)=(-1)^{\langle\gamma,\delta\rangle_{\mathrm{DSZ}}}\varepsilon(\gamma)\varepsilon(\delta)$. Define the physical KS factor at charge $\gamma$ by

$$\mathcal K_{\gamma,u}(y^\delta)=y^\delta\bigl(1-\varepsilon(\gamma)y^\gamma\bigr)^{\Omega_u(\gamma)\langle\delta,\gamma\rangle_{\mathrm{DSZ}}}.$$

The integer power is interpreted by its formal binomial series in the pointed degree completion. Let $\mathcal S_u$ be the composition of these factors over the stable BPS support in decreasing phase order, with the largest phase leftmost. Finally assume an exact model-specific bridge: there is a continuous group homomorphism $\Theta$ from units of the physical completed quantum torus to continuous automorphisms of the commutative charge series, and for every phase $\phi$ and either chamber it satisfies

$$\Theta\!\left(\Phi(J(S_{Z_u}(\phi)))\right)=\prod_{\substack{\gamma\in\Gamma_+\\\phi_u(\gamma)=\phi}}^{\searrow}\mathcal K_{\gamma,u}^{\Omega_u(\gamma)}.$$

Here $S_{Z_u}(\phi)$ and $J$ are the semistable phase factor and skew integration from the finite-field Hall definition. Then

$$\mathcal S_{u_-}=\mathcal S_{u_+}.$$

This is a conditional transport theorem. The specified per-phase bridge is an additional physical input; neither the finite-field Hall identity nor this theorem asserts that the pure-SU(2) model supplies it, that the resulting index counts exist, or that the model has a continuum quantum-field-theory construction.

## Statement references

Physical BPS charge and second-helicity index data: [[def-qftx-physical-bps-charge-data]].

Planned exact Hilbert-space BPS-index interface; its carrier is currently absent: [[def-qftx-physical-bps-index]].

