## Facts & Assumptions

**Given:** $\mathrm{AC}_\omega$, the physical charge/index datum, the finite acyclic quiver and its finite-field stability data, the charge/pairing map, the completed tori, and the stated bridge maps.

[A1] Assume Countable Choice, $\mathrm{AC}_\omega$: every at most countable family of nonempty sets has a choice function. It is inherited through the physical trace-class index-data interface; the finite-field Hall theorem itself is choice-free. [[def-countable-choice]]

[F1] [[def-qftx-physical-bps-charge-data]]: on a regular patch the formal label lattice is $\mathbb Z^2$, $z_u(n_e,n_m)=\sqrt2(n_ea+n_ma_D)$, the chosen DSZ form is integral and antisymmetric, and $\Omega_u(\gamma)$ is the second-helicity supertrace on the supplied one-particle BPS sector.

[F2] [[def-qftx-physical-bps-index]]: the exact Hilbert-space sector, conserved-charge operators, and trace domain are the planned physical index interface. Its item carrier is absent from the current page-53 manifest, so this proof is conditional on that exact interface being instantiated compatibly with the second-helicity trace in [F1].

[F3] [[def-qftx-hall-spectrum-generator]]: for a finite acyclic quiver over $\mathbb F_q$, vertex charges in $\mathbb H$ define semistable subobject-first factors $S_Z(\phi)$ and the degreewise formal skew generator $P_Z^{\mathrm{sk}}=\prod_{\phi}^{\searrow}J(S_Z(\phi))$ in the completion with skew Euler pairing; no physical interpretation is part of this definition.

[F4] [[prop-qftx-hall-spectrum-invariance]]: for any finite acyclic $Q$ over $\mathbb F_q$ and two upper-half-plane vertex-charge assignments, the completed skew generators are equal units. Its inspected proof uses the finite-field HN factorization and continuous skew integration; it proves no physical Hilbert-space identification.

[A2] The common coefficient embedding $\sigma$, charge map $\rho$, degree condition, and continuous factor-matching homomorphism $\Theta$ in the Statement are the exact bridge hypothesis. They include the equality of every Hall phase image with the physical KS factors, not merely a matching of total charge labels.

[A3] The positive cone, finite sublevels, integral indices, and locally finite support in the Statement are assumed so each formal binomial factor and each ordered product is defined degreewise.

## Proof

**Given:** The hypotheses and conventions in the Statement and [F1]–[F4], [A1]–[A3].

1.1 For a supported charge $\gamma$, the series $1-\varepsilon(\gamma)y^\gamma$ has constant term $1$, so it is a unit in the pointed completion; every integer power in $\mathcal K_{\gamma,u}$ is therefore a well-defined formal binomial series. Bilinearity of $\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_{\mathrm{DSZ}}$ gives $\mathcal K_{\gamma,u}(y^{\delta+\delta'})=\mathcal K_{\gamma,u}(y^\delta)\mathcal K_{\gamma,u}(y^{\delta'})$, and $\mathcal K_{\gamma,u}$ fixes $y^\gamma$ because $\langle\gamma,\gamma\rangle_{\mathrm{DSZ}}=0$. Replacing $\Omega_u(\gamma)$ by $-\Omega_u(\gamma)$ gives its inverse. Local finiteness in [A3] makes the ordered composition $\mathcal S_u$ continuous and well-defined. [F1, A3, given, algebra]

1.2 The formula for $\Phi$ preserves products on basis monomials: $\Phi(x^{\mathbf d}*x^{\mathbf e})=\sigma(t)^{-\langle\mathbf e,\mathbf d\rangle_Q}Y^{\rho(\mathbf d+\mathbf e)}$, while $\Phi(x^{\mathbf d})\star_\hbar\Phi(x^{\mathbf e})=\hbar^{-\langle\rho(\mathbf e),\rho(\mathbf d)\rangle_{\mathrm{DSZ}}}Y^{\rho(\mathbf d+\mathbf e)}$. The pairing identity and $\sigma(t)=\hbar$ make these expressions equal. The degree condition in the Statement makes $\Phi$ continuous on the completions. [A2, A3, given, algebra]

2.1 The finite-field hypotheses of [F4] hold for the same $Q$ and the two assignments $Z_{u_-},Z_{u_+}$, since their vertex values lie in $\mathbb H$ by the common phase rotation. Therefore $P_{Z_{u_-}}^{\mathrm{sk}}=P_{Z_{u_+}}^{\mathrm{sk}}$ as units of the completed Hall skew torus. [F3, F4, given]

2.2 Apply the continuous homomorphism $\Phi$ from step 1.2 to the degreewise equality in step 2.1. Equal coefficients remain equal under the coefficient embedding and charge map, so $\Phi(P_{Z_{u_-}}^{\mathrm{sk}})=\Phi(P_{Z_{u_+}}^{\mathrm{sk}})$. [A2, step 1.2, step 2.1]

3.1 Since $\Theta$ is a continuous group homomorphism on units, applying it to step 2.2 preserves equality. Degreewise continuity and local finiteness in [A3] let us pass from the finite phase truncations to the full products. The phase-factor compatibility in [A2] identifies the two images with $\mathcal S_{u_-}$ and $\mathcal S_{u_+}$, respectively, in the same order; [F1], [F2], and [A1] provide the exact BPS index data and its stated choice-strength premise. Thus $\mathcal S_{u_-}=\mathcal S_{u_+}$. [A1, A2, A3, F1, F2, step 2.2] ∎

## Remarks

The equality above is a model-conditional deduction from a separate finite-field Hall theorem and the explicit per-phase bridge. The Hall proposition's own published verification stamp and the current owner proof inspection are kept distinct from the missing physical bridge and from the absent page-53 index carrier.
