### Dated frontier scan (2026-10-23)

An arXiv API search was run on 2026-10-23. Only metadata and abstracts were
read; no full text, peer review, proof or independent priority check was done.
It gives useful *candidate* frontier updates, not accepted results:

- Omar Kidwai and Guillaume Tahar, “Spectral networks, finite webs, and the
  `T_3` cubic differential,” arXiv:2610.23752v1, submitted 2026-10-16,
  `https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.23752v1`. The abstract claims a precise finite-web
  definition and results for one cubic differential on `P^1` with three
  double poles. Full-text review is needed before using any theorem or its
  physical dictionary.
- “Refined Vafa–Witten invariants for toric surfaces from supersymmetric
  localization in 5D gauge theory,” arXiv:2607.18410v1, submitted 2026-07-20,
  `https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.18410v1`. The abstract says the relation of its
  even-first-Chern-class partition function to rational refined Vafa–Witten
  invariants remains unclear. Treat that as the authors' preprint status, not
  a community-wide resolution.
- “Localizing the M-Theory Path Integral,” arXiv:2609.31829v2, abstract
  updated 2026-10-07, `https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.31829v2`. The authors call

3. **Integrations and signs.** The source product is subobject first, f⋆g(L)=sum over U⊆L of f(U)g(L/U), opposite to the generic quotient-first Hall product. Associativity counts the same embedded two-step flags on either parenthesization; the zero object is the unit. The extension ratio is q^(−χ_Q(e,d)), where d=dim U,e=dim V. Thus I(κ_U⋆κ_V)=q^(−χ(e,d))X^(d+e), exactly the Euler target. For J the exponent is −2χ(e,d)+χ(d+e,d+e)=χ(d,d)+χ(e,e)−⟨e,d⟩, with ⟨e,d⟩=χ(e,d)−χ(d,e), confirming the skew product and diagonal factor. Bilinearity gives both twist cocycle identities. This checks the two distinct normalizations rather than conflating their tori.

4. **Completion and wall crossing.** A fixed output dimension uses finitely many dimension decompositions, finitely many representation classes per degree and finitely many phases of vectors 0<e≤d. The ordered product is therefore defined by finite degree truncations, even if the full phase set is infinite or nondiscrete. In decreasing phase order, iterated subobject-first multiplication counts embedded flags with prescribed nonzero semistable factors. Zero factors correspond uniquely to skipped phases. Unique HN gives coefficient exactly 1 on every representation, so the product is A_all. Both degree-preserving integrations commute with these finite truncations; their images of A_all are independent of Z. A series P=1+G with positive-degree G has two-sided inverse sum (-G)^n degree by degree. Conjugation is consequently continuous and unchanged when Z changes. The local proposition uses precisely these products and adds no stronger conclusion.

The scope is every finite acyclic quiver Q (including wild quivers and multiple arrows), finite-dimensional F_q representations, q a prime power >1, and arbitrary vertex charges in the *strict* upper half plane. Semistability includes strictly semistable objects. The coefficient field for the integrated targets is Q(sqrt(q)), t=sqrt(q)>0; completion is over nonnegative dimension vectors with total-dimension filtration. This is the supplied completed positive-degree algebra convention, not an unqualified completion over all lattice directions. No genericity, finite representation type, analytic convergence, 3CY structure, potential, orientation or physical state-counting premise is needed for this finite-field conclusion. No extension to arbitrary cyclic quivers with relations, a different coefficient theory, or continuum QFT has been proved here.

## Consumers and remaining obligations

| Consumer | Exact checked use and disposition |
|---|---|
| `def-qftx-physical-bps-charge-data` | Inventory external edges request the finite-quiver generator/invariance and CY3 bridge *as abstract mathematics*. The invariance edge is currently conditional on upstream reconciliation. The inspected proofs resolve that scientific concern for planning; root may bind this evidence in its owner disposition. Author the named model's charge lattice, pairing, central charge, chamber and protected Hilbert-space index explicitly. These objects are not produced by the finite-field counts. |
| `pthm-qftx-physical-bps-wall-crossing` | Its registered direct prerequisites are charge-data and `def-qftx-physical-bps-index`, both formulation prerequisites. A definition alone proves no wall-crossing identity. Preserve the contract's model-specific protected-index theorem and its separate comparison obligation. Supply an actual physical derivation or an explicit adopted bridge premise and a complete conditional transport proof with matching normalizations/completions. Keep readiness unresolved if that proof/premise is absent. |
| `def-qftx-cy3-bps-integration-contract` | Existing mathematical consumer of the proposition and reused by the charge-data contract. Its finite-field reference is sound after this inspection. It lists required 3CY/heart/stability, orientation, coefficient, integration and protected-state comparison inputs; it asserts neither existence nor a physical bridge. Its other CoHA prerequisites were not audited here. |
| `def-qftx-spectral-network-data` | The inventory has no direct Hall item edge; its page requires the physical wall-crossing page. Author the curve/cover/ramification, meromorphic differential, phase trajectories, junction/finite-web rules, lifted charge and framing independently. No geometric network or physical index follows from the Hall identity. |
| `ex-qftx-t3-finite-web-index` | On the B companion; no registered Hall item premise. Preserve full-text/current-status and source-qualified class-S/T3 calculation obligations. Historical GMN caveats and the abstract-only 2026 lead remain unresolved source obligations. This review does not certify a finite-web index computation or general algorithm. |

Both physical wall-crossing A/B pages and spectral-network A/B pages inherit the scoped mathematical-context disposition; they retain all their own authoring/review obligations. The spectral page dependence is not evidence of an unregistered direct Hall theorem use.

There is **no confirmed gap in the finite-field mathematical proofs**. The smallest additional step for an eventual physical inference is a *model-specific comparison*, not another HN or Hall lemma: identify a well-defined protected Hilbert-space index and its charged/chamber data with the chosen algebraic phase factors, matching charge map, skew pairing, signs/refinement, product order and completion. A simple finite-field identification needs an actual coefficient/torus map taking every relevant factor to its physical factor; continuity and multiplicativity then transport the equal products, and invertible images transport conjugations. Prove these hypotheses for the named model or state them honestly as adopted premises. A CY3/critical-CoHA route instead requires its own integration/factorization theorem with its actual coefficient and orientation hypotheses before the same transport step. The existing bridge definition is a checklist for this work, not its proof.

This preserves the full approved finite-field mathematical scope and the intended model-specific physical coverage. It does not silently replace physical wall crossing by finite counts, classify missing authoring as an open problem, or claim physical realization. Only this report and its JSON evidence were written; no native gates or transitions were run.

