# Batch 54 authoring notes — Hall Wall Crossing and Physical BPS Dictionary

Run: `advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23`
Batch: 54
Scope: `qftx-physical-hall-bps-wall-crossing` and its examples companion only.

## Plan and batch evidence

The canonical plan row matches the full design section at
`research/plan-advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry-track.md:751`: title, category/library, order 1010, reciprocal A/B identity, and all three A-page requirements agree with `research/plan-spec.json` and the assigned manifest. The plan and manifest item arrays are empty placeholders while the design lists the two A items `def-qftx-physical-bps-charge-data` and `pthm-qftx-physical-bps-wall-crossing`. There is no plan-spec conflict. The owner direction requires a substantive B example, so this batch adds one B-only example without changing the shared plan.

`research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-dependency-levels.json` records batch 54 at level 7, requiring batches 33 and 53 (both level 6). These levels set priority, not a wait barrier. The qftx finite-Hall page is an already-present mathematical supplier, not an in-run batch-level edge.

Before authoring, the actual Step-1 records were checked with `loadStep1Record` and `step1Decision`. Current batch-33 items `def-qftx-n2-coulomb-branch-data`, `post-qftx-n2-seiberg-witten-effective-solution`, and `pthm-qftx-n2-bps-central-charge-mass` each have a current `ready` record. Their actual statements and relevant source-normalization interfaces were read. The record for `def-qftx-graded-trace-class-index-data` in batch 1 is also current and `ready`; its statement supplies a pure-point graded trace-class Witten-index datum with an explicit `AC_omega` premise. The assigned page-53 item `def-qftx-physical-bps-index` is absent from the current batch-53 manifest and has no local carrier or readiness record. Its exact planned interface in `research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/proposed-inventory.json` is: define the Z2-graded Hilbert space, supercharge, conserved charges, trace-class supertrace, and exact sector counted by the chosen Witten/helicity index; it depends on `def-qftx-graded-trace-class-index-data`. The carrier is owned by batch 53 and is not authored here.

The current physical math carrier `prop-qftx-hall-spectrum-invariance` is published and has its own `verification.verified` stamp. Its exact proof and the cited finite-field HN, Euler/skew integration, phase, and extension-orbit suppliers were inspected. Those mathematical suppliers' published labels have only `verification.precheck: pass`; the current owner review `research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/hall-review.md` independently checked their complete relevant arguments and found the finite-field chain sound at its stated scope. This review is not relabelled as audit or proof acceptance. The finite-field branch uses finite acyclic quivers over `F_q`, degreewise Hall groupoids, and formal Euler/skew tori; it supplies no Hilbert-space index or physical BPS dictionary. The physical comparison remains a separate explicit bridge premise.

## Source work and claim boundary

Full source files inspected for the assigned physical conventions:

- N. Seiberg and E. Witten, `https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/9407087v1`, Sections 1 (equations 1.1–1.2), 4 (equations 4.3–4.9), and 6 (equations 6.19–6.28). This supports the source-normalized mass/period map, local periods, and alignment/stability discussion. It does not assert every formal lattice label is a stable state or construct a continuum QFT.
- David Tong, `https://davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/supersymmetric-field-theory/susy.pdf`, the full 237-page lecture-note PDF, Section 2.4.2 (printed pages 40–41). It supports the massive N=2 central-charge bound and shortened multiplet; Tong's normalization is not silently substituted for the local Seiberg–Witten convention.
- Frederik Denef, `https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/0206072`, the full 47-page paper, Section 5.3 (printed pages 35–36). It gives the pure-SU(2) monopole/dyon two-node, two-arrow quiver, intersection product of magnitude 2, and chamber-dependent stability in a quiver D-brane/quantum-mechanics description. Its complex quiver moduli are not the finite-field groupoid in the Hall supplier.
- Davide Gaiotto, Gregory W. Moore, and Andrew Neitzke, `https://arxiv.org/pdf/0807.4723`, the full 66-page paper, Introduction equation 1.1, Sections 2.1–2.2, and the opening of Section 7. This supplies the second-helicity supertrace and classical KS factor convention. The paper requires a support condition, distinguishes the physical index from generalized DT invariants before a comparison, and describes its own physical derivation as physical-level rigor; it is context, not a proof that the finite-field Hall count equals the selected SU(2) index.

The earlier specialist notes `research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-localization-bps.md` and `research-supersymmetry.md` and the current owner Hall review were checked for exact reuse limits. No retrieval failure has occurred. Source-fetch stamps and scoped validators remain pending.

## Checkpoint after item 1

Authored `def-qftx-physical-bps-charge-data` on the A page. It defines the regular-patch pure-SU(2) charge-label lattice, the source-normalized scalar central charge, the selected DSZ form, a chamber/wall, a stable one-particle BPS sector, and the second-helicity supertrace. In particular, `gamma_m=(0,1)` and `gamma_d=(1,-1)` have DSZ pairing 2, matching a two-arrow quiver with arrows from the dyon vertex to the monopole vertex. It explicitly does not assert that any label is realized. Natural units are `c=hbar=1`; `a`, `a_D`, and the scalar central charge have mass dimension one.

Direct dependencies and provisional item level:

- `def-qftx-n2-coulomb-branch-data` (formulation prerequisite; batch 33 level 6; current ready record).
- `post-qftx-n2-seiberg-witten-effective-solution` (physical assumption; batch 33 level 8; current ready record).
- `def-qftx-physical-bps-index` (formulation prerequisite; absent page-53 carrier; its planned dependency `def-qftx-graded-trace-class-index-data` has level 1, hence planned supplier level 2).
- `def-countable-choice` (mathematical premise; carries only `AC_omega` inherited from the planned trace-class index data).

Thus the item level is provisionally 9. Its exact B2 index use remains conditional on the missing page-53 carrier matching the recorded planned interface. No claim of readiness is made; record it `escalated` after finishing all assigned authoring.

Next action: author the conditional Hall-to-physical KS transport theorem with exact coefficient, charge, pairing, phase-order, completion, and factor-matching hypotheses; then complete the two-arrow finite-field B example. After both, finalize manifests, proof contracts, coverage, source stamps, dependency rows, scoped checks, and Step-1 records.

## Checkpoint after item 2

Authored pthm-qftx-physical-bps-wall-crossing as a conditional transport theorem. It defines the physical second-helicity KS automorphisms, the finite-quiver skew torus, the coefficient/charge map, pairing and degree compatibility, and the per-phase bridge needed to identify each Hall factor with the physical index factor. Its proof first checks the formal KS factors are continuous automorphisms, applies the inspected finite-field Hall invariance proposition, proves the torus map preserves products from the coefficient and DSZ/skew-pairing identities, and transports the completed equality through the bridge. No physical count is derived from Hall data without that explicit bridge.

Direct prerequisites are def-qftx-physical-bps-charge-data, the planned def-qftx-physical-bps-index (page 53, carrier absent), def-qftx-hall-spectrum-generator and prop-qftx-hall-spectrum-invariance (published mathematical carriers inspected at their exact finite-field interface), plus def-countable-choice for the inherited AC_omega trace-data assumption. The coefficient map is required to send sqrt(q) to the physical quantum-torus parameter; the charge map preserves the exact DSZ/skew form and completion degree. The bridge's realization of B2 indices as images of finite-field Hall phase factors remains unproved and is deliberately an explicit hypothesis. Source treatments read: GMN, Introduction/Section 2.2 for B2 and KS factors (its physical derivation is not used as the local proof); Denef Section 5.3 for model-specific SU(2) monopole/dyon quivers; Seiberg–Witten Sections 4 and 6 for charge periods and alignment. Source-fetch stamps and proof-contract generation remain pending.

The provisional item level is 10: one plus the maximum in-run supplier level, the charge-data item at 9. The missing page-53 index item's planned direct mathematical supplier has level 1, hence planned item level 2, below the maximum. This is consistent with batch 54's level 7 page dependencies on batches 33 and 53. Current loadStep1Record/step1Decision evidence shows the batch-33 Coulomb and Seiberg–Witten items are ready; the BPS-index carrier is absent. This item must be recorded escalated after completion.

## Checkpoint after item 3

