items/pthm-qftx-physical-bps-wall-crossing.md:110:1.2 The formula for $\Phi$ preserves products on basis monomials: $\Phi(x^{\mathbf d}*x^{\mathbf e})=\sigma(t)^{-\langle\mathbf e,\mathbf d\rangle_Q}Y^{\rho(\mathbf d+\mathbf e)}$, while $\Phi(x^{\mathbf d})\star_\hbar\Phi(x^{\mathbf e})=\hbar^{-\langle\rho(\mathbf e),\rho(\mathbf d)\rangle_{\mathrm{DSZ}}}Y^{\rho(\mathbf d+\mathbf e)}$. The pairing identity and $\sigma(t)=\hbar$ make these expressions equal. The degree condition in the Statement makes $\Phi$ continuous on the completions. [A2, A3, given, algebra]
items/pthm-qftx-physical-bps-wall-crossing.md:112:1.3 The finite-field hypotheses of [F3] hold for the same $Q$ and the two assignments $Z_{u_-},Z_{u_+}$, since their vertex values lie in $\mathbb H$ by the common phase rotation. Therefore $P_{Z_{u_-}}^{\mathrm{sk}}=P_{Z_{u_+}}^{\mathrm{sk}}$ as units of the completed Hall skew torus. [F2, F3, given]
items/pthm-qftx-physical-bps-wall-crossing.md:114:2.1 Apply the continuous homomorphism $\Phi$ from step 1.2 to the degreewise equality in step 1.3. Equal coefficients remain equal under the coefficient embedding and charge map, so $\Phi(P_{Z_{u_-}}^{\mathrm{sk}})=\Phi(P_{Z_{u_+}}^{\mathrm{sk}})$. [A2, step 1.2, step 1.3]
