+- `item-dependency-levels.mjs check` reports no batch-55 item mismatch. It still reports seven unrelated level mismatches in batch 61: `lem-aqft-local-counterterm-shift-is-relative-coboundary` (0 vs 3), `def-aqft-thooft-anomaly` (0 vs 3), `def-aqft-anomaly-matching-data` (1 vs 4), `pthm-aqft-selected-chiral-spectrum-anomaly-cancellation` (2 vs 5), `ex-aqft-single-chiral-fundamental-polynomial` (2 vs 5), `ex-aqft-mixed-background-counterterm-shift` (2 vs 5), and `ex-aqft-vectorlike-conjugate-chiral-pair` (3 vs 6). These are outside this batch's write scope.
+- `batch-dependency-levels.mjs check` reports the shared run-level snapshot stale after manifest authoring. Recompute from current manifests confirms batch 55 still schedules at page level 8 and requires batches 36 and 54; the shared snapshot is owner/global evidence and is not changed here.
+- Fresh readiness snapshots show all inspected item inputs current and ready: `def-aqft-topological-defect`, `def-aqft-topological-interface`, both required Hall-page items, and `def-qftx-physical-bps-index` (the latter was inspected but is not used). Current non-owner Step 1 records now mark `def-qftx-spectral-network-data` and then `ex-qftx-t3-finite-web-index` ready in supplier-first order; the B record includes the current A item hash. These are authoring-readiness records only, not independent proof acceptance.
